# Root schema for the Contract Management service.
#
# The GraphQL specification requires a schema to declare a `Query` root, even when the
# service exposes nothing to read. This service currently exposes nothing at all: the
# tour-booking example and the `mlc` context were deleted together, and the `contract`
# context specified in documentation/use-cases/uc01-create-master.spec.md and its siblings
# has not been built yet.
#
# So the root carries one infrastructure field rather than a domain read. Inventing a domain
# query here would ship a read side that no spec asked for and no use case owns — and UC02
# (GetMaster) is the spec that owns the first real one.
#
# The first increment of the `contract` context replaces this field, and adds its operations
# by `extend type Mutation` against the root declared below.
type Query {
    "Version of this API. Not a domain read."
    apiVersion: String!
}
